From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 16:26:03 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] drm/asahi: g16: Drop the runtime and suspend-to-idle
 RTKit idles

g16_rt_idle_ms and g16_s2idle_idle put the GPU firmware's RTKit into
idle (AP and IOP 0x201) with its power kept and woke it with
apple_rtkit_wake(). That round trip doesn't exist on this firmware: the
idled ASC stops its CPU, and a firmware stopped that way only comes
back through the warm restart after a real sleep, as sleep_hold() here
and apple_rtkit_sleep_return() already say. On the J604 the first wake
after a runtime idle timed out (IOP power acknowledgment -ETIME) and
the device fail-stopped.

Nor is it what macOS does at runtime: with no management message sent
for the whole idle, macOS has the GPU domain gated 98.6-99.9% of the
time, so its idle power-off is the firmware's own.

Remove both parameters and their paths. The power-assert count accessor
stays for g16_wake_restore.

This reverts 5147481ad2 ("drm/asahi: g16: Optionally idle the
firmware's RTKit when the GPU is idle") and 8d55dbfe2e ("drm/asahi:
g16: Optionally idle the firmware's RTKit at suspend-to-idle").

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
